{"id":"60c58ee2-cad1-49a8-9c61-54f894d0bda6","object":"chat.completion","created":1784992425,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n['parent']\\n        if p is not None:\\n            children.setdefault(p, []).append(n['id'])\\n    all_ids = [n['id'] for n in nodes]\\n    candidates = [n for n in nodes if n['removable'] and n['symbol'] not in required_symbols]\\n    candidates.sort(key=lambda x: (-x['depth'], x['id']))\\n    removed_set = set()\\n    removed_order = []\\n    for node in candidates:\\n        nid = node['id']\\n        if nid in removed_set:\\n            continue\\n        child_list = children.get(nid, [])\\n        if any(c not in removed_set for c in child_list):\\n            continue\\n        ok = True\\n        for sym in required_symbols:\\n            found = False\\n            for n2 in nodes:\\n                if n2['id'] != nid and n2['id'] not in removed_set and n2['symbol'] == sym:\\n                    found = True\\n                    break\\n            if not found:\\n                ok = False\\n                break\\n        if not ok:\\n            continue\\n        removed_set.add(nid)\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n    retained = sorted([nid for nid in all_ids if nid not in removed_set])\\n    return {'removed_node_ids': removed_order, 'retained_node_ids': retained}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for SE-PE-01. The task is \"grammar_guided_node_reduction\". The input case contains a tree of nodes with fields: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. Also required_symbols list. The goal is to select nodes to remove (those that are removable) while preserving that all required symbols remain represented in the remaining tree. Also need to consider grammar validity? The problem mentions \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates\" but given the simplified scaffold, likely the rule is: we cannot remove a node if it would cause a required symbol to be missing from the tree (i.e., no node with that symbol remains). Also we cannot remove root (removable false). The algorithm: sort nodes by depth descending (deeper first), then by id as tie-breaker. For each node that is removable, tentatively remove it if after removal, all required symbols are still present in the set of retained nodes (including root and non-removable nodes). Also need to consider children: \"never remove a node with retained children\" - i.e., if a node has children that are retained, we cannot remove it? Actually \"a node with retained children\" means the node has children that are not removed? The instruction: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" So we cannot remove a node if it has any child that is retained (i.e., not removed). But if we are processing deeper nodes first, we might remove children first, then parent becomes childless. However the rule says \"retained children\" meaning children that are still in the tree after removals. So we must check at the moment we consider removing a node: if any of its children are still present (i.e., not removed), we cannot remove it. So effectively we can only remove leaf nodes? Not necessarily: if all children are removed (or were not present), then parent can be removed if it meets other conditions. But children removal happens first because deeper nodes considered first. So algorithm: process nodes in descending depth. Maintain set of removed nodes. For each node (skip root, non-removable), check: if it is removable, if any child (based on parent field) is not removed (i.e., still retained), then skip. Else, check if after removing it, all required symbols are still present in the set of nodes that are not removed (including this node temporarily? we simulate removal). If yes, then remove it. Finally, return retained_node_ids (all nodes not removed) sorted, and removed_node_ids in the order of removal (the order we removed them). The output schema requires arrays of strings. So implement solve(case) accordingly.\n\nConstraints: use only stdlib, no external randomness, no file access, etc.\n\nWe'll write Python code. The input case is the payload object: has \"nodes\" list and \"required_symbols\" list. We'll parse.\n\nImplementation steps:\n- Build a dict of nodes by id for easy access.\n- Build a set of node ids that are not removable (including root) but we can just filter by removable flag.\n- Determine initial set of retained node ids: all node ids. Then we'll remove some.\n- We need to process nodes in order: sort by depth descending, then by id as tiebreaker (stable). Among nodes that are removable, and not already removed.\n- For each candidate:\n    - Check if any child (nodes with parent == this id) is still retained (i.e., not removed). If yes, skip.\n    - Check if all required symbols are still present if we remove this node: i.e., among retained nodes (excluding this one), do we have at least one node with each required symbol? Also need to consider that the removed node might be the only one with that symbol? But we have required_symbols that must be preserved. So compute: after removal, for each required symbol, there must be at least one retained node with that symbol. Since root has symbol \"root\", required symbols typically include \"root\" and maybe some others. So if this node is the only node with a required symbol, we cannot remove it.\n    - If both conditions satisfied, remove it: add to removed list, remove from retained set.\n- After processing all, sort retained_node_ids list (all node ids not removed) and sort removed_node_ids in removal order (the order we accumulated them). Return dict with those two arrays.\n\nNote: \"never remove ... a